  "comment": "MTG_EXEC_CLEAN_BP_DEFERRED (2026-10-20, docs/design/rollout-executor-lockstep.md #18). Hinata s12111487 gi 486's T5 board (MTG_HINATA_GAMBLE_PAST_DORK=1, shipped d5 b30), the Soulfire dig's staged cards held as hand cards. The kill: main 1 Izzet Boilerworks (the deferred Karoo) + Soulfire Eruption with a REMAND rider -- Remand counters it back to hand and draws Reality Spasm -- then, AFTER the Karoo, the Spasm untaps the Boilerworks among six sources; main 2 Soulfire again, Spasm, Preordain + Remand, Preordain, Sol Ring, Ponder, Irencrag Feat, Crackle with Power. The cast is non-opaque, so the executor runs it through its CLEAN-set loop, which used to replay the Remand's continuation at the cast: the Spasm then ran BEFORE the Karoo, untapped the Island the Boilerworks bounced, the Boilerworks stayed tapped and main 2 was two mana short (no win, opponent at 8). The rollout defers a plain cantrip's continuation past the Karoo; the executor now does too. MTG_EXEC_CLEAN_BP_DEFERRED=0 fails this fixture (also at --depth 8 --budget-ms 0)."
